Start new Codex sessions with approvals and the sandbox bypassed.

codex_bypass_approvals (OMNIGENT_CODEX_BYPASS_APPROVALS=1) was meant to do
this through codex-wrapper.sh, but upstream's codex-native host starts the
app-server with a cleaned environment that drops the variable, and its TUI
asks for workspace-write with auto review. Codex then ran inside its own
seccomp sandbox: no network, no DNS, no tailnet. Upstream's switch for this
is the omnigent.codex_native.bypass_sandbox session label (#657), opt-in
from the new-session form.

Where the deployment turns bypass on, a new codex-native session that gave
no bypass label and no approval or sandbox launch flags gets the label "1".
A client that sets the label, "0" included, or passes --sandbox,
--ask-for-approval or --full-auto keeps its choice. GET /v1/info says
codex_bypass_default, so the web form can start on Bypass and send "0" for
another preset (web-patches/0025-codex-bypass-default.patch).
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0016-startup-progress.patch.
